{
  "opportunity_id": "proc_11b4cf2680",
  "source": "content_cluster",
  "title": "Correcting wrong deal prices by hand in Sitara",
  "task_class": "deal_entry_correction",
  "label_mechanical": "Deal entry and correction in Sitara / Unify / TAGG: correct deal / price / sitara",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Someone notices that the price recorded against a specific deal number in Sitara does not match what was actually agreed or billed \u2014 often surfacing when a settlement, invoice, deal summary or flash report is reviewed. That person mails the deal number, the flow date and the price it should be to whoever has write access, usually phrased as \"can you please update the deal in Sitara\". The holder of access edits the deal and replies to confirm the adjustment, and in some cases also checks a second place \u2014 another trading system or a spreadsheet \u2014 so the two agree. The thread ends with an acknowledgement that the price now reads correctly; occasionally the original deal cannot be amended and a fixed price is written onto the lines instead as a workaround.",
    "where_it_stalls": "The correction is a mail round-trip between the person who spotted the bad price and the person allowed to change it, so nothing moves until that second person answers. Every message in this cluster carries a rework signal and most carry manual transfer: the price is retyped from mail into Sitara, and then again into the other system or sheet, with no automatic reconciliation between them. Corrections also arrive late \u2014 after billing or after a deal summary has already been produced \u2014 and at least one thread shows a price being revised more than once because the first correction was not the final agreed number.",
    "why_it_recurs": "Prices enter Sitara by hand at deal capture, downstream reports and invoices are the first place an error becomes visible, and each reporting cycle surfaces a fresh batch of mismatches to fix by mail.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A scheduled comparison between the deal price in Sitara and the corresponding price in the downstream system or settlement sheet, flagging mismatches by deal number and flow date before the deal summary or invoice goes out. Pair it with a standing correction form that captures deal number, date, hours and corrected price so the edit can be applied and logged without a mail exchange.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
